UMBRA: An Automated System for Analyzing Cookie Consent Interfaces

UMBRA is an automated system for large-scale analysis of evolved dark patterns in cookie consent interfaces. 
It detects banners, interacts with their UI elements, and monitors cookie behavior across multiple interaction 
states to identify regulatory and security-related violations.
The system is capable of automatically identifying nine advanced categories of dark patterns (DP11–DP19), 
including transparency failures, opt-out pricing, revocation barriers, and consent circumvention behaviors.

## Prerequisites

The system requires the following software to be installed:

Python 3.8 or higher (tested with Python 3.9+)

Google Chrome (latest stable version recommended)

ChromeDriver (matching the installed Chrome version)

 ## Installation

Run the following commands inside the directory containing requirements.txt.

(Recommended) Create a Virtual Environment

Windows

python -m venv umbra_env
umbra_env\Scripts\activate


Linux / macOS

python3 -m venv umbra_env
source umbra_env/bin/activate

## Install Dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

## Usage
cd Source_code
python run_auto.py


